{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365657-question-about-goetia","id":1365657,"title":"Question about goetia.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-05T21:07:35-08:00","id":1365657,"title":"Question about goetia.","content":"Ok,so here's what I know about Goetia. They show up in the Temenos when a group of people believe in the same idea. And they reflect that idea.<br /> However,what happens when an idea that people have contradicts the nature of the Astral Realms?<br /> For instance. Let's say long ago there was a civilization who believed in a God. That God was the leader of their pantheon in their worshipper's mind. Extremely powerful in their minds. The people who truly loved and worshipped that god believed him to be the top dog of creation itself.<br /> But here's the problem,only 300 people truly believed in that god. That creates only an rank 2 Goetia. There's a contradiction,the few people who believe the god think he is extremely powerful, mightiest being in the Universe. But by the astral's rules,he's just an rank 2 goetia. How does that work? Does the goetia know it's not as powerful as their worshipper's believe? Is the goetia even aware that he is not the ruler of the cosmos? How self aware is he? And powers he does have?<br /> Edit: that same line of questione kinda works for superheroes too doesn't it? If a few people read a comic about a superhero who can punch through a mountain,but he's only an rank 2 goetia,how does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 02-06-2020, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T21:19:53-08:00","id":1365658,"title":"","content":"Goetia are a broader category than that. Your Oneiros has goetia in it for example, even though you don't share that with anyone. What pops up in the Temenos when more than one person is thinking about a thing is a whole Temenotic Realm. It can be filled with goetia, or not have any, and that's largely dependent on the nature of the realm itself.<br /> <br /> The goetia you're asking about would in fact be the most powerful goetia in the realm it inhabits since it's believed to be all powerful by its believers. It's most likely going to be unaware of its actual status as not all that powerful, unless it receives information from outside of its realm, which not many goetia do, though a god is in a better position than most. Even if it knows though, since it represents its believers ideas of god it will act as if it is that god and stick to behavior appropriate to its role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T21:22:24-08:00","id":1365659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365657-question-about-goetia?p=1365658#post1365658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goetia are a broader category than that. Your Oneiros has goetia in it for example, even though you don't share that with anyone. What pops up in the Temenos when more than one person is thinking about a thing is a whole Temenotic Realm. It can be filled with goetia, or not have any, and that's largely dependent on the nature of the realm itself.<br /> <br /> The goetia you're asking about would in fact be the most powerful goetia in the realm it inhabits since it's believed to be all powerful by its believers. It's most likely going to be unaware of its actual status as not all that powerful, unless it receives information from outside of its realm, which not many goetia do, though a god is in a better position than most. Even if it knows though, since it represents its believers ideas of god it will act as if it is that god and stick to behavior appropriate to its role.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is it correct to say that what the people believe doesn't make the goetia more powerful,just how many people believe it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T21:30:52-08:00","id":1365662,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of Temenos residents are barely Rank 1, if that.<br /> <br /> Numina for the most part aren't locked to Rank minimums and goetia in particular are mechanically required to spend their Numina slots on Numina, since they don't Manifest and their Influence is pretty purely descriptive, so most of the grand powers of a given Temenotic goetia are going to live in that chunk of their statblock.<br /> <br /> Creating a whole new part of the Temenos requires that the idea be both sufficiently resonant and sufficiently distinct from other ideas, or else they end up in the same part of the Temenos as similar ideas and the mess has to sort itself out; variations on the same archetype are approximately equal in power and may make war on each other for dominance in the collective unconscious as a literalized abstraction of the conflict between their respective ideas in the minds of their &quot;believers.&quot;<br /> <br /> In theory, at least, such a goetia is broadly aware that he needs to seize more mental territory and become more prominent in the landscape of the human soul if he is to overcome the limits of his station and live up to his story, but without more differentiation from similar &quot;gods&quot; he's liable to run into interference from variations on his theme who've got the same idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T21:36:16-08:00","id":1365663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365657-question-about-goetia?p=1365662#post1365662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast majority of Temenos residents are barely Rank 1, if that.<br /> <br /> Numina for the most part aren't locked to Rank minimums and goetia in particular are mechanically required to spend their Numina slots on Numina, since they don't Manifest and their Influence is pretty purely descriptive, so most of the grand powers of a given Temenotic goetia are going to live in that chunk of their statblock.<br /> <br /> Creating a whole new part of the Temenos requires that the idea be both sufficiently resonant and sufficiently distinct from other ideas, or else they end up in the same part of the Temenos as similar ideas and the mess has to sort itself out; variations on the same archetype are approximately equal in power and may make war on each other for dominance in the collective unconscious as a literalized abstraction of the conflict between their respective ideas in the minds of their &amp;quot;believers.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In theory, at least, such a goetia is broadly aware that he needs to seize more mental territory and become more prominent in the landscape of the human soul if he is to overcome the limits of his station and live up to his story, but without more differentiation from similar &amp;quot;gods&amp;quot; he's liable to run into interference from variations on his theme who've got the same idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm getting it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T06:45:03-08:00","id":1365713,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the Superhero point, I imagine the realms of the Temenos that these sort of Goetia are going to inhabit the general rules of it are going to be larger than life, buildings breaking like they were cardboard, cars being casually thrown etc. Think on how absurd the feats of some of the human characters in a superhero universe are then imagine what a realm constructed from 100s of people reading these narratives would be like.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the Diety aspect. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I remember correctly the section on Goetia and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tenemos </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bis very succinct, and considering other factors than just number of believers when stating them up might help to a degree. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I wouldn't think it would be unreasonable to increase or decrease the rank of a Goetia depending on how important, and formed it is to those who believe in it (and possibly also having a modifier for how long they have been believed in) would all be a sensible considerations if you want a Tenemos that is less distorted by modern meme culture and the internet (Which is probably good for most Mage Games). Also the spirit/goetia scale doesn't match well with the rest of the game. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThat 'all powerful' diety is still likely to be slaughtered in a direct fight by the Goetia of Justin Beiber, but it at least gives it a bit more bite.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","user":"mcgonigle","date":". 02-06-2020, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","name":"mcgonigle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:28:07-08:00","id":1365883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mcgonigle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365657-question-about-goetia?p=1365713#post1365713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the Superhero point, I imagine the realms of the Temenos that these sort of Goetia are going to inhabit the general rules of it are going to be larger than life, buildings breaking like they were cardboard, cars being casually thrown etc. Think on how absurd the feats of some of the human characters in a superhero universe are then imagine what a realm constructed from 100s of people reading these narratives would be like.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On the Diety aspect. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I remember correctly the section on Goetia and the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tenemos </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bis very succinct, and considering other factors than just number of believers when stating them up might help to a degree. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I wouldn't think it would be unreasonable to increase or decrease the rank of a Goetia depending on how important, and formed it is to those who believe in it (and possibly also having a modifier for how long they have been believed in) would all be a sensible considerations if you want a Tenemos that is less distorted by modern meme culture and the internet (Which is probably good for most Mage Games). Also the spirit/goetia scale doesn't match well with the rest of the game. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThat 'all powerful' diety is still likely to be slaughtered in a direct fight by the Goetia of Justin Beiber, but it at least gives it a bit more bite.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>So ,worship does has some effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T17:17:47-08:00","id":1365897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365657-question-about-goetia?p=1365883#post1365883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So ,worship does has some effect</div> </div> </div> </div>Belief, not worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T17:36:44-08:00","id":1365899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1365657-question-about-goetia?p=1365897#post1365897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Belief, not worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think I got you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}